Domain Entity AssessmentFamily
    documentation 'This entity represents a logical grouping or association of assessments that 
                  'share a common purpose, heritage or content standard. There may be hierarchies
                  'of assessment families, characteristics (e.g., Academic Subject) specified for 
                  'assessment families, by convention, are inherited by the Assessments associated 
                  'with the AssessmentFamily.
    shared string AssessmentTitle named AssessmentFamilyTitle
        documentation 'The title or name of the AssessmentFamily.
        is part of identity
        is queryable field
    include AssessmentFamilyIdentificationCode
        documentation 'A unique number or alphanumeric code assigned to an assessment family by a 
                      'school, school system, a state, or other agency or entity.
        is required collection
        is queryable field
    descriptor AssessmentCategory
        documentation 'The category of an assessment based on format and content. For example: 
                      'Achievement test, Advanced placement test, Alternate assessment/grade-level 
                      'standards, Attitudinal test, Cognitive, and perceptual skills test, etc.
        is optional
        is queryable field
    descriptor AcademicSubject
        documentation 'The description of the content or subject area (e.g., arts, mathematics, 
                      'reading, stenography, or a foreign language) of an assessment family.
        is optional
    descriptor GradeLevel
        documentation 'The typical grade level for which an assessment family is designed. If the 
                      'assessment spans a range of grades, then this attribute holds the highest grade 
                      'assessed. If only one grade level is assessed then only this attribute is used. 
                      'For example: Adult, Prekindergarten, First grade, Second grade, etc.
        is optional
        with context Assessed
    descriptor GradeLevel
        documentation 'If the assessment spans a range of grades, then this attribute holds the lowest 
                      'grade assessed. If only one grade level is assessed, then this attribute is 
                      'omitted.
        is optional
        with context LowestAssessed
    include ContentStandard
        documentation 'An indication as to whether an assessment conforms to a standard (e.g., local 
                      'standard, statewide standard, regional standard, association standard).
        is optional
    descriptor Language
        documentation 'An indication of the languages in which the AssessmentFamily is designed.
        is optional collection
    shared integer Version named Version
        documentation 'The version identifier for the AssessmentFamily.
        is optional
        is queryable field
    date RevisionDate
        documentation 'The month, day, and year that the conceptual design for the AssessmentFamily 
                      'was most recently revised substantially.
        is optional
    string Nomenclature
        documentation 'Reflects the specific nomenclature used for this level of AssessmentFamily.
        is optional
        min length 1
        max length 35
    descriptor AssessmentPeriod
        documentation 'The periods or windows defined in which an assessment is supposed to be 
                      'administered.
        is optional collection
    reference AssessmentFamily
        documentation 'References the higher level AssessmentFamily the AssessmentFamily belongs to.
        is optional
        with context Parent
    shared string URI named Namespace
        documentation 'Namespace for the Assessments in this AssessmentFamily.
        is required